WEBVTT

00:10:28.493 --> 00:10:30.303
was a virtue,

00:10:30.327 --> 00:10:33.557
but one, I think,
that is perhaps less aspirational

00:10:33.581 --> 00:10:35.510
and a lot more confrontational

00:10:35.534 --> 00:10:39.169
than the one that people
who talk about civility a lot today

00:10:39.193 --> 00:10:40.495
tend to have in mind.

00:10:40.519 --> 00:10:44.153
So I like to call that virtue
"mere civility."

00:10:45.288 --> 00:10:49.138
You may know it as the virtue
that allows us to get through

00:10:49.162 --> 00:10:51.598
our relations with an ex-spouse,

00:10:51.622 --> 00:10:53.130
or a bad neighbor,

00:10:53.154 --> 00:10:55.455
not to mention a member
of the other party.

00:10:55.973 --> 00:11:01.206
Because to be merely civil
is to meet a low bar grudgingly,